      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SPACE_DETAIL\n- SPACE_FLOOR\n\n## Column Mapping\n- floor: SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_NAME\n- Stata building: SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_KEY\n- building 32: SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_KEY\n- largest room square footage: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n- largest room name: SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME\n- rooms loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24: SPACE_DETAIL.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\n- room square footage greater than 100: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n- space unit: SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_NUMBER\n- room square footage greater than 10: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n- building room name: SPACE_DETAIL.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME\n- room number: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_NUMBER\n- room square footage: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n- average room square footage within the floor: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n- average room square footage per floor: SPACE_DETAIL.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\n\n## Join Keys\n- SPACE_DETAIL.FLOOR_KEY <-> SPACE_FLOOR.FLOOR_KEY\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Stata building\" is predicated by \"TABLE.BUILDING_NAME = 'Ray and Maria Stata Center'\"\n- \"Stata building\" is predicated by \"TABLE.BUILDING_KEY = '32'\"\n- \"Stata building\" is predicated by \"TABLE.BUILDING_KEY = '32'\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each floor, what is the largest room square footage and the name of the building room with that largest square footage, for rooms loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24, with a largest room square footage greater than 100, and only for rooms in the Stata building (building 32)?\n```sql\nSELECT sf.FLOOR_NAME, sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd JOIN SPACE_FLOOR sf ON sd.FLOOR_KEY = sf.FLOOR_KEY WHERE sd.BUILDING_KEY = 32 AND sd.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24' AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE > 100 AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE = ( SELECT MAX(sd2.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE) FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd2 WHERE sd2.BUILDING_KEY = 32 AND sd2.FLOOR_KEY = sd.FLOOR_KEY AND sd2.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24' ) ORDER BY sf.FLOOR_NAME;\n```\n2. For each space unit in the Stata building with a room square footage greater than 10, show the building room name, room number, room square footage, floor name, and the average room square footage within each floor, ordered by room square footage.\n```sql\nSELECT sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, sd.ROOM_NUMBER, sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, sf.FLOOR_NAME, AVG(sd2.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE) AS AVG_ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE_PER_FLOOR FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd JOIN SPACE_FLOOR sf ON sd.FLOOR_KEY = sf.FLOOR_KEY JOIN SPACE_DETAIL sd2 ON sd2.FLOOR_KEY = sd.FLOOR_KEY WHERE sd.BUILDING_KEY = 32 AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE > 10 GROUP BY sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, sd.ROOM_NUMBER, sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, sf.FLOOR_NAME ORDER BY sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each floor in the Stata building (building 32), what is the largest room square footage and the name of the building room with that largest square footage for rooms loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24 with a largest room square footage greater than 100, and for each space unit on that floor with a room square footage greater than 10, what are the building room name, room number, room square footage, and the average room square footage within the floor? List the results showing floor name, largest room name, largest room square footage, building room name, room number, room square footage, and average room square footage per floor, ordered by floor name and room square footage. Do not return any rounded answers."
