      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Database access is denied for direct verification, so I'll rely on the strong precedent metric `dw_2528` in the semantic network, which is the same question shape (minus the floor warehouse load date column).\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n- **SPACE_DETAIL** (table): Space assignment detail fact table — one row per physical room assigned to a space unit. Key columns: `BUILDING_KEY` (FK to FCLT_BUILDING; building 32 = Stata), `FLOOR_KEY` (FK to SPACE_FLOOR), `BUILDING_ROOM_NAME`, `ROOM_NUMBER`, `ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE` (area in square feet), `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE` (DD-MON-YY text; all current rows carry '19-DEC-24').\n- **SPACE_FLOOR** (table): Lightweight floor lookup — one row per floor key with `FLOOR_KEY`, `FLOOR`, `FLOOR_NAME` (verified unique: 49 names for 49 rows), `WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE`.\n- **dw_2528** (metric): \"Stata Building Per-Floor Largest Room with Room-Level Square Footage and Floor Average\" — an almost identical question, adding only the floor warehouse load date column. Its SQL is the direct precedent.\n- **concept_room_space_inventory** / **concept_floor_inventory** (concepts): group SPACE_DETAIL among room-inventory tables and SPACE_FLOOR among floor tables respectively.\n- **column_concept_space_unit_key**, **column_concept_building_room** (column concepts): document SPACE_UNIT_KEY and BUILDING_ROOM identifier semantics; not needed for the requested output columns.\n- Other Phase 1 results (BUILDINGS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD, FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, FCLT_FLOOR, FAC_FLOOR, SPACE_UNIT, etc.) are alternative room/floor sources from other table families; the question's column mapping explicitly anchors to SPACE_DETAIL/SPACE_FLOOR, so they are excluded from use.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- SPACE_DETAIL joins: SPACE_FLOOR (via FLOOR_KEY), SPACE_UNIT, FCLT_BUILDING, SPACE_USAGE, BUILDINGS, SPACE_UNIT2.\n- SPACE_FLOOR: joined by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY; member of concept_floor_inventory.\n- dw_2528 lineage: depends on SPACE_DETAIL and SPACE_FLOOR only.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n- **Floor source**: SPACE_FLOOR (lightweight lookup, has FLOOR_NAME, joins SPACE_DETAIL directly) vs FCLT_FLOOR/FAC_FLOOR (area-rich, different key families, no direct join to SPACE_DETAIL). The question asks for FLOOR_NAME → SPACE_FLOOR is the only candidate with that column and the documented join key.\n- **Room source**: SPACE_DETAIL (square footage in sq ft, has WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE, BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, ROOM_NUMBER) vs FCLT_ROOMS/FAC_ROOMS (area in square meters, different keys) vs ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (no area measures). All requested measures exist only in SPACE_DETAIL.\n- **Task-requirement fitness**: SPACE_DETAIL + SPACE_FLOOR SUPPORT every atomic requirement (floor name, largest room name/sqft with 19-DEC-24 and >100 filters, per-room name/number/sqft with >10 filter, per-floor average, ordering). Alternatives NOT-SUPPORTED (missing FLOOR_NAME join or sq-ft measure).\n- **Wording anchoring**: \"loaded into the warehouse on 19-DEC-24\" → SPACE_DETAIL.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE (room-side filter per documented column semantics); \"Stata building (building 32)\" → BUILDING_KEY = 32; \"average room square footage within the floor\" → AVG over self-join on FLOOR_KEY (precedent dw_2528 computes it over all rooms sharing the floor key, without the >10 or building filter on the sd2 side).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\ndw_2528 is the documented precedent for exactly this question shape; it uses two CTEs (largest room per floor; room + floor average) joined on FLOOR_NAME.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n- SPACE_DETAIL: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓\n- SPACE_FLOOR: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓\n- dw_2528: semantic_get ✓ (full SQL precedent)\n- Concepts/column concepts from search: reviewed via descs; not required for output columns.\n- mysql_query verification: attempted repeatedly — access denied (1045), so verification relies on the precedent metric SQL.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\nUse SPACE_DETAIL ⋈ SPACE_FLOOR on FLOOR_KEY, following dw_2528's structure exactly, dropping the floor warehouse load date column (not requested here). SELECT list: FLOOR_NAME, largest room name, largest room square footage, BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, ROOM_NUMBER, ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, AVG per floor; ORDER BY floor name, room square footage. No rounding.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_921e8bf46f424be1908ae736",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "submit_SQL",
            "arguments": "{\"sql\": \"WITH largest_room_per_floor AS (\\n  SELECT sf.FLOOR_NAME,\\n         sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME,\\n         sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE,\\n         sd.FLOOR_KEY\\n  FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd\\n  JOIN SPACE_FLOOR sf ON sd.FLOOR_KEY = sf.FLOOR_KEY\\n  WHERE sd.BUILDING_KEY = 32\\n    AND sd.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24'\\n    AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE > 100\\n    AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE = (\\n          SELECT MAX(sd2.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE)\\n          FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd2\\n          WHERE sd2.BUILDING_KEY = 32\\n            AND sd2.FLOOR_KEY = sd.FLOOR_KEY\\n            AND sd2.WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE = '19-DEC-24'\\n        )\\n),\\nroom_and_avg_per_floor AS (\\n  SELECT sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME,\\n         sd.ROOM_NUMBER,\\n         sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE,\\n         sf.FLOOR_NAME,\\n         AVG(sd2.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE) AS AVG_ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE_PER_FLOOR,\\n         sd.FLOOR_KEY\\n  FROM SPACE_DETAIL sd\\n  JOIN SPACE_FLOOR sf ON sd.FLOOR_KEY = sf.FLOOR_KEY\\n  JOIN SPACE_DETAIL sd2 ON sd2.FLOOR_KEY = sd.FLOOR_KEY\\n  WHERE sd.BUILDING_KEY = 32\\n    AND sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE > 10\\n  GROUP BY sd.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME, sd.ROOM_NUMBER, sd.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE, sf.FLOOR_NAME, sd.FLOOR_KEY\\n)\\nSELECT lrf.FLOOR_NAME,\\n       lrf.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME AS LARGEST_ROOM_NAME,\\n       lrf.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE AS LARGEST_ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE,\\n       raf.BUILDING_ROOM_NAME,\\n       raf.ROOM_NUMBER,\\n       raf.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE,\\n       raf.AVG_ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE_PER_FLOOR\\nFROM largest_room_per_floor lrf\\nJOIN room_and_avg_per_floor raf ON lrf.FLOOR_NAME = raf.FLOOR_NAME\\nORDER BY lrf.FLOOR_NAME, raf.ROOM_SQUARE_FOOTAGE\"}"
          }
        }
